NV_PK(26,{"mi gao is made from wheat flour":"","it is made from sticky rice":"","you need cucumber to make tainan sticky rice mi gao":"","you need mung beans to make tainan sticky rice mi gao":"","it is also called the koxinga fish tainan has farmed it for hundreds of years":"","this is the swamp eel that lives in rice fields it is not the eel used in japanese eel rice":"","the chinese name sounds like korea but one story says it comes from kool the dutch word for cabbage":"","its name sounds like higher every year so people eat it at the lunar new year":"","long sticky rice is for salty dishes like zongzi round sticky rice is for sweets like mochi":"","americans usually say shrimp the british often say prawn":"","wasabi has been grown on alishan since the japanese period":"","clay pot duck is the signature of a mei an old taiwanese restaurant in tainan it is a dish that takes a lot of time and skill and the restaurant has been making it for sixty years a clay pot is a thick pot made of baked clay it keeps heat well so it is good for slow cooking":"","the most special thing is how it is cooked the dish is named after a clay pot but the restaurant uses an iron pot on a traditional stove with charcoal the owner says a gas stove cannot make the same special smell":""});